                                        "sense_id": "f8c7634d-a7f1-3782-88f4-8630b4e235c0",
                                        "entry_id": "c1ee96d4-fbf6-313f-9e65-bc093bb3af2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female singer or chanter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92ec6cf5-d94c-465f-9de4-2caa4be1b724",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c7634d-a7f1-3782-88f4-8630b4e235c0",
                                                "text": "Thee Chauntress, oft the woods among / I woo, to hear thy even song."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6800ddf6-59e1-484f-bd22-0dacf8f7ee78",
                                                "sense_id": "f8c7634d-a7f1-3782-88f4-8630b4e235c0",
                                                "text": "On this occasion the abbess' kitchen had to provide each lady of the convent with half a goose, the two chantresses, as well as the four usual recipients, receiving doubles, and with a hen or a cock, the fratresses and the subprioress also receiving doubles."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e99c47b-980b-4c6e-9b53-51c6e0d177e1",
                        "source_entry_id": "147a089c-9ab1-3de3-aef3-b8a8e30a1d92",
                        "source_sense_id": "205d578f-08e5-3a68-b964-b1b11addb90f",
                        "target_lang_word": "songstress",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "songstress",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7272415-5321-3bc6-97f9-0236a281c4d9",
                                        "entry_id": "10fa2c82-992b-3ea9-a605-a2463c49af36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female singer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32bf415c-a294-437f-81ad-aafeab99e7dc",
                                                "sense_id": "d7272415-5321-3bc6-97f9-0236a281c4d9",
                                                "text": "At every pause in the music she gracefully waved her flower-basket round, inviting the loiterers to buy; and many a sesterce was showered into the basket, either in compliment to the music or in compassion to the songstress—for she was blind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2994a52-25fd-44b6-bce1-9d588f0dc118",
                                                "sense_id": "d7272415-5321-3bc6-97f9-0236a281c4d9",
                                                "text": "The songstress paused, and was answered by one or two deep and hollow groans, that seemed to proceed from the very agony of the mortal strife."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c69bf2c4-2374-4722-bdce-878853471090",
                                                "sense_id": "d7272415-5321-3bc6-97f9-0236a281c4d9",
                                                "text": "Were I to reproduce the nine other paragraphs, it would be a very curious, instructive, and tedious specimen of literature; and, who knows? I might corrupt some immaculate soul, inspire some actor or actress, singer or songstress, with an itch for public self-laudation, a foible from which they are all at present so free. Witness the Era, the Hornet, and Figaro."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fda5688-afef-4f3c-ae04-7b31a5ab6655",
                                                "sense_id": "d7272415-5321-3bc6-97f9-0236a281c4d9",
                                                "text": "Sally Yeh is the winsome and amiable character known as Stool, who’s living next door to the ambitious and tetchy songstress Shu-Shu, who’s both commanding and funny as portrayed by Sylvia Chang."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d40cb14-3e31-361f-a792-b18ddad01065",
                                        "entry_id": "10fa2c82-992b-3ea9-a605-a2463c49af36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A female songbird."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "96c3e56b-2221-4f96-8ef3-e5a09b5c2d05",
